{"_id":"68a736358ec3d8323af1dda5","nodeId":"PskCueCc9pSxfnSzfdX-u","roadmapSlug":"rust","createdAt":"2025-08-21T15:07:32.844Z","description":"# Vector\n\n`Vec<T>` is Rust's growable, heap-allocated array that stores elements of the same type contiguously. Unlike arrays, vectors can resize at runtime. Key methods include `push()` to add elements, `pop()` to remove the last element, and `len()` for size. Example: `let mut v = vec![1, 2, 3];`","resources":[{"type":"official","title":"Vector","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/std/vec/struct.Vec.html","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdc90"},{"type":"official","title":"Storing Lists of Values with Vectors","url":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch08-01-vectors.html?highlight=vector#storing-lists-of-values-with-vectors","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdc91"},{"type":"article","title":"Rust Vector (With Examples)","url":"https://www.programiz.com/rust/vector","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdc92"},{"type":"video","title":"Rust Vectors","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nOKOFYzvvHo&t=97s&pp=ygUMcnVzdCB2ZWN0b3Jz","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdc93"},{"type":"video","title":"Common Collections in Rust","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Zs-pS-egQSs&t=39s&pp=ygUMcnVzdCB2ZWN0b3Jz","_id":"6a7f4b36cb44947debcfdc94"}],"updatedAt":"2026-08-14T17:07:02.070Z","lessonPacks":[],"paidResources":[],"contribution":"https://github.com/kamranahmedse/developer-roadmap/tree/master/roadmaps/rust/content/PskCueCc9pSxfnSzfdX-u.md"}